From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:40:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/43] qt: track the mouse over the native Wayland video
 window

On Wayland the video is a native child window, whose mouse events reach
the video widget through its event filter. The widget did not track the
mouse, so Qt dropped every move without a button: the controls of the
full screen never came back when the mouse moved, as they do on X11,
where the video widget already tracks it.

Track the mouse on the window container and on the video widget. Double
clicks already reached the video output, which enters and leaves the
full screen.

First written by Daniel Ramos as patch 3d-0027 of the A10 field build
(vlc-stereo 3.0.24-1+stereo3d11~a10.1, 19 October 2026).

Assisted-by: GPT-6 Astra via Codex
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 modules/gui/qt/components/interface_widgets.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/gui/qt/components/interface_widgets.cpp b/modules/gui/qt/components/interface_widgets.cpp
index c9b6100..cda76ee 100644
--- a/modules/gui/qt/components/interface_widgets.cpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/components/interface_widgets.cpp
@@ -134,6 +134,10 @@ bool VideoWidget::request( struct vout_window_t *p_wnd )
         video->installEventFilter(this);
         stable = QWidget::createWindowContainer(video, this);
         stable->setFocusPolicy(Qt::StrongFocus);
+        /* The native child's mouse moves reach this widget through the
+         * event filter: without tracking, Qt drops those with no button */
+        stable->setMouseTracking(true);
+        setMouseTracking(true);
         layout->addWidget(stable);
         stable->show();
         video->create();
